text:
clara: Quick a11y note from a keyboard + SR pass on the model version picker (left column + inline actions). Two surprises: focus jumps when switching versions with keyboard, and VoiceOver sometimes reads the wrong rollout state after a quick swap. Posting short repros.

diego: Thanks. Repro steps? I haven't seen the VO mismatch locally.

clara: On staging: tab to a model row, press Enter to open inline version menu, ArrowDown to choose v2, press Enter. Expected: focus stays on the chosen menu item or the updated version label, and VO announces "Version v2 active". Observed: focus moves to the top of the list and VO sometimes announces the previous version or nothing. Seems timing-related when the row re-renders.

hannah: I can reproduce on mac+VO and NVDA. When the version change triggers a small re-render the active element is replaced, and the SR announces the next DOM sibling name instead. Also noticed the inline menu uses role="menu" but the items are buttons, which confuses some SRs.

aria-bot: Auto hints: avoid restoring focus to nodes that may be replaced. Use a focus-anchor or focus-retention id; prefer real <menuitem> semantics or use a simple <ul>/<button> pattern with aria-checked/aria-current for active versions. Ensure a single live-region announces state changes, e.g. "Version v2 active".

diego: Plan: 1) change inline menu markup to <ul role="listbox"> + <li role="option"> so we get predictable selection semantics; 2) before applying version swap, insert a temporary focus-anchor span next to the row (tabindex=-1) and focus it; after the DOM update, move focus to the new version label or keep it on the anchor, then remove anchor. 3) emit a single polite announcement from central announcer: "Activated version v2 for Model X".

clara: Nice. Also copy nit: the visible toggles read "Activate" and we also had aria-label="activate version" on the icon; VO read duplicate "Activate button activate version". Remove redundant aria-labels on visible text.

hannah: Validation plan: keyboard-only flow for version swap, VO/NVDA confirm correct announcement order, ensure role/listbox semantics work, and contrast for inline menu items in dark theme. I'll run tests after PR.

diego: Pseudocode for the anchor flow:
```
const anchor = document.createElement('span');
anchor.tabIndex = -1; anchor.id = `focus-anchor-${rowId}`;
row.after(anchor);
anchor.focus({preventScroll:true});
// perform version swap update
// after render or on next animation frame:
const newLabel = document.getElementById(`version-label-${rowId}`);
if (newLabel) newLabel.focus({preventScroll:true});
anchor.remove();
```

aria-bot: Suggestion: use requestAnimationFrame or MutationObserver to wait for the DOM update before moving focus to avoid announcing wrong node. Also use aria-live="polite" on the central announcer for single messages.

clara: Sounds good. Owners: Diego (impl), Hannah (QA). Acceptance checklist for PR: keyboard activation keeps focus predictable, no duplicate SR labels, central live-region announces "Activated version <x> for <model>", listbox/option roles used consistently, and dark/light contrast check for menu items.

diego: I'll open a small PR with markup changes, focus-anchor util, and announcer message. Tagging @hannah for validation.

hannah: Will run VO/NVDA matrix and keyboard tests once PR is up. Also will test fast repeat swaps to ensure stable announcements.

clara: Thanks team — goal is predictable keyboard-first versioning with clear SR feedback and no DOM-timing surprises. :thumbsup:
